      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockaway_Beach%2C_Queens",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1878, landowner Holland donated parcels to the New York, Woodhaven and Rockaway Railroad, sparking the peninsula’s first station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockaway_Beach%2C_Queens",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Surfing returned to Rockaway Beach in the late 1960s, drawing artists and restaurateurs who turned the area into a year‑round hotspot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityneighborhoods.nyc/rockaway-beach",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Temple of Israel Synagogue, built in 1921, earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places in 2014.",
